====================================================================================================
 (2) THE SIGN + THE BANKED DATED SIGN-FLIP (D3 lane, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21179352)
====================================================================================================
  memory times carried (both): channel-M Lorentzian tau=0.45 Gyr; E10 covariant tau=2c/a0=203 Gyr (tau*H_L=2Z=11.578).
  Cluster crossing time T_cross ~ 2-3 Gyr ~ few x tau_M -> the memory transient is a
  RESOLVABLE infall-phase signal (not frozen), unlike the deep-adiabatic star-orbit lane.

  SIGN STRUCTURE across pericentre (fiducial theta0=2, canonical a0):
    POST-peri (recent plunge, y_cur=0.60,y_hist=1.50, t=0.50Gyr,w=0.33): y_eff=0.90 -> EXCESS   +2.2%  (HOTTER than settled twin)
    PRE-peri  (first infall,  y_cur=0.90,y_hist=0.10, t=0.30Gyr,w=0.51): y_eff=0.49 -> DEFICIT  -2.9%  (COOLER than settled twin)
  ==> THE SIGN-FLIP (banked, dated, pre-registered D3 'No Pump-Free Corner'):
      first-infall / pre-peri members run a DEFICIT (memory of the cold isolated past);
      recent post-peri backsplash members run an EXCESS (memory of the hot pericentre).
      MI-UNIQUE: tides can only HEAT (never a deficit) and never flip sign across peri;
      MG gives IDENTICAL sigma for all three phases. The sign-flip is the cleanest tag.
  ==> BASELINE SIGN (settled band): plungers/backsplash HOTTER, first-infall COOLER;
      the raw y-loading (shed-adiabatic) makes high-omega_ex members hotter at fixed radius.

