====================================================================================================
 (4) DEPENDENCE ON CLUSTER MASS + MEMBER DEEP-MOND DEPTH
====================================================================================================
  (a) CLUSTER MASS sets the shell radius and crossing time; the fractional spread AT a
      fixed (a_ex/a0, a_in/a0) is MASS-INDEPENDENT. Amplitude is set by member depth, not
      cluster mass; mass moves the carrier zone outward and lengthens the memory window.
      M_cl=1e+14: shell R(a_ex=a0)=0.39 Mpc, sigma_cl~747 km/s, T_cross~1.0 Gyr = 2.2 x tau_M (memory resolved: YES)
      M_cl=3e+14: shell R(a_ex=a0)=0.67 Mpc, sigma_cl~983 km/s, T_cross~1.3 Gyr = 3.0 x tau_M (memory resolved: YES)
      M_cl=1e+15: shell R(a_ex=a0)=1.22 Mpc, sigma_cl~1328 km/s, T_cross~1.8 Gyr = 4.0 x tau_M (memory resolved: YES)
  (b) MEMBER DEEP-MOND DEPTH -- who carries it (y=omega_ex/omega_in per member class):
      UDG   sig=15 Re=3.0: a_in= 0.03 a0 | y_plunge= 2.00 y_circ=0.133 -> spread ~ 13.7%
      dSph  sig=10 Re=1.0: a_in= 0.03 a0 | y_plunge= 1.00 y_circ=0.067 -> spread ~  7.0%
      dE    sig=50 Re=1.5: a_in= 0.58 a0 | y_plunge= 0.30 y_circ=0.020 -> spread ~  0.5%
      L*ell sig=200 Re=4 : a_in= 3.46 a0 | y_plunge= 0.20 y_circ=0.013 -> spread ~  0.1%
  ==> ONLY diffuse deep-MOND members (UDG/dSph, low omega_in) reach y~1 and carry the
      6-13% spread. dE / L* ellipticals are ADIABATIC-DEAD (y<<1, internally Newtonian)
      -> ~0 spread. The SDSS/DESI-sigma-measurable members are exactly the DEAD ones:
      this is the power wall (banked POWER_cluster_efe_channel.md), not the prediction.

